dra: available
  status:   Kubernetes gates: alpha in 1.34-1.35, beta default-on in 1.36 (DRAExtendedResource GA in 1.37)
  families: all: NVIDIA, Intel GPU and Gaudi DRA drivers, CPU (dra-driver-cpu)
  value:    partitionable devices, consumable capacity, binding conditions, extended-resource requests served by DRA, device health in pod status
image-volume: available
  status:   Kubernetes ImageVolume: beta default-off in 1.33-1.34, beta default-on from 1.35
  families: all: models shipped as OCI images, mounted read-only into any accelerator pod
  value:    model weights pulled, cached and deduplicated by containerd; no init-container copy or PVC
ov-kv-cache: available
  status:   OpenVINO 2026.4.0 property KV_CACHE_PRECISION, OVMS 2026.4.1 --kv_cache_precision; off by default
  families: CPU (every Core and Xeon) and Intel GPU (iGPU, Arc, Arc Pro)
  value:    u8 KV cache: more concurrent agent sessions or longer context in the same memory
ov-dynamic-quant: available
  status:   OpenVINO 2026.4.0 property DYNAMIC_QUANTIZATION_GROUP_SIZE (0 = off); off by default
  families: CPU (AMX/VNNI Xeon, Core) and Intel GPU
  value:    int8 activations on weight-compressed LLM matmuls: lower prefill latency for tool-call loops
npu-turbo: available
  status:   OpenVINO 2026.4.0 NPU property NPU_TURBO; ivpu sched_mode param (HW scheduler auto-selected on new firmware)
  families: Intel NPU: Meteor/Arrow Lake (37xx), Lunar Lake (40xx), Panther/Wildcat Lake (50xx), Nova Lake (60xx)
  value:    sustained max NPU clocks for latency-bound agent inference; HW scheduler gives per-context priority and preemption
scx: absent — kernel 6.12.48-1-lts has no /sys/kernel/sched_ext/state (needs Linux 6.12+ built with CONFIG_SCHED_CLASS_EXT)
  status:   sched_ext merged in Linux 6.12; schedulers (scx_lavd, scx_layered) out of tree, sched-ext/scx v1.1.4
  families: any x86 host on Linux 6.12+ with CONFIG_SCHED_CLASS_EXT; most useful on hybrid P/E parts
  value:    latency-aware or layered CPU scheduling for agent processes, swapped at runtime with no reboot
xe-force-probe: absent — no unbound Intel GPU: every Intel GPU on this host already has a driver, or there is none (force_probe only helps a GPU the kernel did not bind)
  status:   xe.force_probe (unsafe param, taints the kernel); Nova Lake-P and Crescent Island still need it in Linux 7.3-rc
  families: Intel GPUs the running kernel will not bind: Nova Lake-P, Crescent Island, MTL/ARL/ADL/TGL/DG2 on xe
  value:    brings a new GPU up before distro kernels support it, so agents can schedule on it
xe-sriov: absent — no Intel GPU bound to xe reports SR-IOV (sriov_totalvfs missing or 0; needs a PF-capable part, CONFIG_PCI_IOV, xe.max_vfs not 0 and VT-d on)
  status:   xe SR-IOV PF: xe.max_vfs param, configfs sriov/max_vfs since Linux 6.19; PF on BMG and PTL without force_probe
  families: Panther/Wildcat Lake iGPU, Battlemage / Arc Pro B, Nova Lake, Crescent Island (bound to xe)
  value:    hardware-isolated GPU slices: each VF is its own render node and gpu.intel.com/xe resource
